Description: system control for odio: upgrades, components, DAC, web UI
 odioctl drives an odio installation from the command line and from a small
 LAN web UI:
 .
  * odioctl upgrade check|apply|verify — the odios upgrade path (state.json
    vs published manifest, INSTALL_*/RUN_* derivation, install.sh re-run),
    wired to the odio-check-upgrade timer and odio-upgrade service;
  * odioctl components — opt roles and features in or out of the next upgrade;
  * odioctl dac — pick the DAC dtoverlay in the Raspberry Pi config.txt;
  * odioctl web — stdlib HTTP server with a plain-HTML page for the above.
 .
 Ships systemd --user units (not auto-enabled) and a sudoers fragment
 granting the `odio` group the exact privileged commands it needs.
